From: Kerem Karabay <kekrby@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] HID: Apple Touch Bar backlight and keyboard mode (hid-appletb-bl, hid-appletb-kbd), backport to 6.12

Backport of the two Touch Bar HID drivers that are upstream since Linux
6.15, for the Touch Bar of T2 MacBook Pros (2018-2020) reached through the
T2's internal USB (apple-bce VHCI): hid-appletb-kbd puts the Touch Bar in
its "keyboard" mode, where the T2 itself draws Esc + F1-F12 or the media
and brightness keys and reports them as key presses (Fn switches between
the two layers); hid-appletb-bl drives its backlight (dim and off after
inactivity). No DRM driver is needed for this mode; appletbdrm (custom
drawing with tiny-dfr) and the hid-multitouch Touch Bar changes are NOT
part of this patch.

Authors: Ronald Tschalär, Kerem Karabay <kekrby@gmail.com>,
Aditya Garg <gargaditya08@live.com>. Licence: GPL-2.0 (kernel code).

Sources (pinned):
  * drivers/hid/hid-appletb-bl.c, drivers/hid/hid-appletb-kbd.c: copied
    unchanged from Linux v6.18 (https://github.com/torvalds/linux/tree/v6.18,
    the upstream files with the later fixes: probe error path, backlight
    reference put, timer only deleted when it was set up), except one API
    bridge: timer_container_of() (6.16+) -> from_timer() (6.12).
  * Kconfig, Makefile, hid-quirks.c and the sysfs ABI file: from t2linux
    linux-t2-patches commit 7a48a744e190400606a032d4d2b8704ee908fb2c
    (the 6.12 series), patches 1005-HID-hid-appletb-bl-add-driver-for-the-
    backlight-of-A.patch and 1006-HID-hid-appletb-kbd-add-driver-for-the-
    keyboard-mode.patch (https://github.com/t2linux/linux-t2-patches),
    plus upstream's "depends on X86 || COMPILE_TEST".

Carried by IYAKKI for the optional Mac image variant only
(dist/buildroot/configs/iyakki_mac.fragment). Applies to Linux 6.12.112.
